  (text "Y" (at 166.37 159.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 75edfbfd-7b01-471c-9081-00d2cd22be17)
  )
  (text "Input subsystem (pilink-7el.6, amended by pilink-cmn): 2 discrete tact\nswitches (UP/DOWN) + 4 discrete tact buttons (A/B/X/Y) + 1 rotary\nencoder (volume) -- see .planning/decisions/2026-11-14-dpad-instead-of-joystick.md\nfor the original d-pad ADR and .planning/decisions/2026-11-15-rotary-encoder-for-volume.md\nfor the amendment that replaced LEFT/RIGHT with the encoder. The original\nADR replaced a 5-way joystick (UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT/PRESS) with 4\nindividually-plungered switches and no center-press switch; the\n2026-11-15 amendment then replaced the LEFT/RIGHT pair with a single\nEC11-class incremental quadrature rotary encoder with integrated\npushbutton, dedicated to volume (rotate = adjust, press = mute/toggle),\nper user-reported usage data showing LEFT/RIGHT went unused on the\nprototype. There is no PRESS/select net on this sheet -- firmware must\nremap select/OK onto one of A/B/X/Y itself; that remap is firmware's job\n(../pico-link, not this repo) and does not block this hardware design." (at 220 15 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 06d6a717-f00b-43da-b3c4-49d4780d0282)
  )
  (text "Pull resistor convention: each switch gets its own external 10k pull-up\n(R301, R302, R305-R308) from +3V3 to the GPIO node; the switch itself\n(SW301, SW302, SW305-SW308) pulls that node to GND when pressed --\nactive-low, pressed = logic 0. The rotary encoder (SW303) follows the\nsame convention for all 3 of its signals: quadrature channels A and B\nare each externally pulled up to +3V3 (R303, R304) and pulled toward GND\nthrough the encoder's internal mechanical contact against its common pin\nC (wired directly to GND); the integrated push-switch (pins S1/S2) is\nwired the same way -- S2 pulled up to +3V3 through R309, S1 wired\ndirectly to GND (S1/S2 are an unpolarized SPST contact pair per the\ndatasheet, so which terminal is pulled up is an arbitrary but\ndocumented choice, not a functional constraint). Alps' EC11E18244AU datasheet (see part-citation note\nbelow) rates the encoder's contacts at 10mA max / 1mA min and specifies\nno internal pull resistors, so external pull-ups are required exactly as\nfor the discrete switches -- same reasoning as this sheet's original\npull-up note: ordinary GPIOs have no guaranteed default pull state, so an\nexplicit external pull-up keeps each input well-defined independent of\nfirmware GPIO init order. This differs from rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch's\nBOOTSEL/reset switches (SW101/SW102), which rely on the boot-ROM's own\nQSPI_SS handling and RUN's internal pull-up respectively and fit no\nexternal pull-up -- those are special-function pins with documented\ndefault behavior." (at 220 54 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 6405952e-260e-4bf6-8c01-8d8442176dae)
  )
  (text "GPIO net assignment: GPIO20/21/24-27 unchanged (UP=20, DOWN=21, A=24,\nB=25, X=26, Y=27), picked from the generic bidirectional GPIO pool\nrp2350b_memory.kicad_sch exposes as global labels for every RP2350B GPIO\nnot already committed to that sheet's own circuitry (GPIO47/PSRAM_CS is\nthe only pin withheld from that pool). The 2026-11-15 amendment\n(pilink-cmn) reuses the two GPIOs freed by removing LEFT/RIGHT (GPIO22,\nGPIO23) for the rotary encoder's quadrature channels A and B, and claims\none additional GPIO (GPIO28, the next free pin in the pool) for the\nencoder's push-switch -- confirmed free by grepping all 4 populated\nsheets (power, rp2350b_memory, esp32_bt, input) for every GPIO/ESP32_*/\nglobal label before finalizing: no sibling sheet claims GPIO22, GPIO23,\nor GPIO28. Same cross-sheet convention as esp32_bt.kicad_sch's ESP32_*\nglobal labels: sibling child sheets join same-named nets project-wide\nvia a global label, no hierarchical sheet pins or root-sheet wiring\nneeded. Each switch/signal also carries its firmware-facing logical name\n(UP/DOWN/A/B/X/Y, VOL_A/VOL_B/VOL_SW for the encoder) as a plain text\ncaption -- deliberately NOT a second schematic label on the same net: a\nglobal label and a local label both landing on one net connect fine\nelectrically, but ERC reports it as multiple_net_names (the global label\nwins in the netlist either way), so the logical name is\ndocumentation-only graphical text here instead, with no electrical\nmeaning and nothing for ERC to flag." (at 220 109 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 3c0ca8f7-c187-466d-9449-00281f05387b)
  )
  (text "Reference designators use this project's per-sheet numbering block\n300-399 (power.kicad_sch: 1-99, rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch: 100-199,\nesp32_bt.kicad_sch: 200-299) so no two sibling sheets' components can\nmerge into the same netlist part. The 2026-11-15 amendment (pilink-cmn)\nretired SW304 (the old RIGHT switch -- left as an intentional gap, not\nreused) and repurposed SW303 for the new rotary encoder, reusing\nR303/R304 as its two quadrature pull-ups and adding R309 as the\npush-switch's pull-up; #PWR305/#PWR307 (both freed +3V3) and\n#PWR306/#PWR308 (both freed GND) are reused for the encoder's pull-up\nsupplies and direct GND returns (common C via #PWR306, switch pin S2 via\n#PWR308), with one new #PWR317 (+3V3) added for the third pull-up.\nUP/DOWN/A/B/X/Y keep their original SW301/SW302/SW305-SW308,\nR301/R302/R305-R308, and #PWR301-#PWR304/#PWR309-#PWR316 unchanged. No\nPWR_FLAG on this sheet, matching rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch's and\nesp32_bt.kicad_sch's own reasoning -- this sheet doesn't generate\n+3V3/GND, power.kicad_sch does, so a standalone ERC run on this sheet\nalone is expected to report power_pin_not_driven for both rails; the\nroot sheet (which flattens the whole hierarchy and does see the\nregulator) is the real check. See hardware/README.md for both ERC runs\nand the project-wide netlist collision check.\n\nFLAG for firmware integration (out of scope here): firmware's current\nPL_INPUT_PIN_* pin NUMBERS (2/18/16/20/15/17/19/21, the old Waveshare\nboard's GPIO map) still need remapping to this schematic's GPIO\nassignment, and PL_INPUT_PIN_LEFT/PL_INPUT_PIN_RIGHT go away entirely in\nfavor of a new quadrature-decode + push-button read path for the\nencoder -- tracked as follow-up bead pilink-otf (pin remap) plus the\nnot-yet-filed encoder firmware work flagged in\n.planning/decisions/2026-11-15-rotary-encoder-for-volume.md." (at 220 164 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9846e71a-aed5-4181-b0cc-b62ef7d1a9ec)
  )
  (text "Rotary encoder part choice (pilink-cmn): Alps Alpine EC11E18244AU --\nJLCPCB/LCSC C202365, Extended-library part (not Basic -- standard\nextended-part handling fee, not a sourcing-availability risk). Verified\nagainst Alps' own published datasheet (alps.com EC11E18244AU\nbasic-information page, retrieved via LCSC's hosted copy at\nlcsc.com/datasheet/C202365.pdf): Vertical structure, flat actuator,\n20mm actuator length, 36 detents / 18 pulses, two-phase incremental\noutput (terminals A, B, common C), integrated push-on switch (SPST,\n0.5mm travel, 0.1A/5V DC rating, terminals labeled D/E on the datasheet\n-- mapped onto this sheet's S1/S2 pins), 10mA/5V DC max rating overall,\nno internal pull resistors (hence the external pull-ups on all 3\nsignals, see the pull-resistor-convention note above). Symbol: stock\nKiCad library Device:RotaryEncoder_Switch (5 pins: A, B, C, S1, S2 --\nexact match for this part's A/B/C/D/E pinout). Footprint: stock KiCad\nlibrary Rotary_Encoder:RotaryEncoder_Alps_EC11E-Switch_Vertical_H20mm --\nthis exact footprint is purpose-built for an Alps EC11E + integrated\nswitch + vertical mount + 20mm shaft, i.e. this specific part\nfamily/variant, not a generic stand-in. Live stock cross-checked\n2026-11-15 across two independent sources (JLCPCB's own part page\nconfirming Extended-library class, and a third-party LCSC data mirror\nshowing roughly 3.2k units in stock) -- no single authoritative live\nfigure could be scraped directly from LCSC's or JLCPCB's JS-rendered\nproduct pages in this environment, so treat the exact unit count as\napproximate, not a guaranteed snapshot." (at 220 233 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9179a531-c9a3-4f5d-a7fc-337028bcbb9e)
  )
)
